## Why This Is Asked
Assesses end-to-end Azure data plane design: storage, compute, eventing, and governance with real-world tenant isolation and disaster recovery considerations.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant isolation using dedicated Storage Accounts and SQL partitioning with row-level security
- GPU-accelerated processing in AKS with Event Grid-triggered Blob events
- Durable Functions for workflow orchestration
- Canary feature flags via App Configuration
- Cost-aware autoscaling via KEDA
- Cross-region disaster recovery and Purview lineage tracking

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton: Azure Function triggered by Event Grid blob creation
module.exports = async function processUpload(context) {
  const blobPath = context.bindingData.blobTrigger;
  const tenantId = extractTenantId(blobPath);

  const config = await appConfig.getConfiguration(tenantId);
  if (config.canaryEnabled) {
    await applyWatermark(blobPath, config.watermarkSettings);
  }

  await sql.updateMetadata(tenantId, blobPath, 'processed');
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates a junior Azure developer's ability to design multi-tenant APIs with API versioning, schema-driven validation, and environment-aware configuration. It also tests understanding of data isolation patterns and CI/CD pipeline testing strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant data isolation using tenantId as the partition key
- API versioning via the X-API-VERSION request header
- Per-version schema storage in Azure App Configuration
- Version-aware data routing and schema-driven payload validation
- End-to-end testing across dev, stage, and production environments

## Code Example

```javascript
// Version routing sketch
function routeRequest(req) {
  const version = req.headers['x-api-version'] || 'v1';
  const schema = appConfig.get(`schemas.${version}`);

  if (!schema) {
    return { status: 400, body: 'Unsupported API version' };
  }

  const validated = validatePayload(req.body, schema);
  if (!validated.valid) {
    return { status: 422, body: validated.errors };
  }

  return { version, partitionKey: req.headers['tenant-id'] };
}
```

